Package: hphq
Title: Automated Cataloging of Highly Probable Hierarchy Questions (HPHQ)
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
  c(person("Caitlin", "Daly", email = "caitlin.daly@uwaterloo.ca", role = c("aut", "cre")),
  person("Chloe", "Tan", role = "aut"),
  person("Audrey", "Béliveau", email = "audrey.beliveau@uwaterloo.ca", role = "aut"))
Maintainer: Caitlin Daly <caitlin.daly@uwaterloo.ca>
Description: This package implements an efficient computational approach (Daly et 
  al. 2026) that systematically compiles a comprehensive catalog of all highly 
  probable treatment questions (e.g., those with an empirical 
  probability exceeding 95%) that may be asked in the context of network 
  meta-analysis (NMA) or other situations where there is a joint distribution 
  of the relative effects between multiple (>2) treatments.
